   "date": "2013-03-14",
   "stage_hint": null,
   "brief": "The coalition supported the Customs Amendment (Anti-Dumping Commission) Bill 2013 to establish the Australian Anti-Dumping Commission, but criticised the government for belatedly adopting opposition policy and raised concerns about the source of $24.4 million in funding, citing failed anti-dumping cases that cost jobs at Kimberly-Clark, SPC Ardmona and CSR Viridian."
